      "created_at": "2019-04-15T15:09:12Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-04-15T15:09:12Z",
      "body": "> In short, a+b can overflow, but a-b cannot?\r\n\r\nI think it's more that by always checking the elapsed time against `now() - starttime`, you never need to represent the time at which the timeout should happen - which may be so far in the future that it causes a signed overflow.",
