      "created_at": "2021-12-06T13:26:08Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-12-06T13:26:08Z",
      "body": "> I think PR https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/28674 has resolved this issue.\r\n\r\nYou're right.\r\n\r\n\\_threadmodule.c now uses \\_PyDeadline_Init() which calls \\_PyTime_Add(), and \\_PyTime_Add() prevents integer overflows; Extract of its implementation:\r\n\r\n```c\n// Compute t1 + t2. Clamp to [_PyTime_MIN; _PyTime_MAX] on overflow.\r\nstatic inline int\r\npytime_add(_PyTime_t *t1, _PyTime_t t2)\r\n{\r\n    if (t2 > 0 && *t1 > _PyTime_MAX - t2) {\r\n        *t1 = _PyTime_MAX;\r\n        return -1;\r\n    }\r\n    else if (t2 < 0 && *t1 < _PyTime_MIN - t2) {\r\n        *t1 = _PyTime_MIN;\r\n        return -1;\r\n    }\r\n    else {\r\n        *t1 += t2;\r\n        return 0;\r\n    }\r\n}\n```",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
